      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T22:12:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discussing in sidebar. The purpose of the lock is to ensure that mutations don\u0027t result in leaking internal implementation details due to internally inconsistent behavior (IOW, the class misbehaving due to the callback vs throwing behavior in getTransformState()). It\u0027s not to make the class thread-safe; a caller that wants to use the class across multiple threads is responsible for that. Making the class thread safe wouldn\u0027t be expensive, but I don\u0027t want to give the appearance of ConcurrentIpSecTransform. Having to use a lock at all is a somewhat unfortunate state of affairs.",
      "parentUuid": "08b2c785_7ff494cb",
